  "customfield_10187": null,
  "description": "<p>This task is to ensure that \"omitting\" server-managed triples (SMT) behaves as expected under the following circumstances:<br/>\n1) Create an RDF Source with client-provided triples, then request that resource (omitting SMTs) and ensure that only the client-provided triples are in the response.<br/>\n2) Add an rdf:type to the RDF Source, and ensure that it is included in the response that omits SMTs.<br/>\n3) Ensure server-managed triples can not be updated (i.e. repository namespace).</p>\n\n<p>Note: To omit server-managed triples on GET requests, include the following request header:</p>\n<hr />\n<p>Prefer: return=representation; omit=\"http://fedora.info/definitions/v4/repository#ServerManaged\"</p>\n<hr />",
